API  (import: sys.path.insert(0, f"{R}/scripts/nl9"); from cell_nl import CellNeighborList, BatchTemplate, round_cap)
  NL = CellNeighborList(r_max, pbc, cell, n_atoms, E_cap, device="cuda", bin_cap=None, bins_per_dim=None)
  out = NL.build(positions)      # [N,3] fp64 cuda (caller's unwrapped coords). No host sync, no allocation,
                                 # CUDA-graph capturable; 6 kernels in 2 extension calls, no torch ops:
                                 # k_prep (bbox/zero, 1 block) k_bin (atomics into fixed bins) k_wscan<0> (warp per
                                 # dst atom: count) k_rowscan2 (block scan -> rowptr, n_edges, E>E_cap flag)
                                 # k_wscan<1> (ballot-compacted hits -> scratch, slot = rank by sender in row: sorted
                                 # without a sort) k_final (unit_shifts/shifts, reverse-edge binary search -> perm_src,
                                 # padding)
  out (persistent buffers, overwritten by the next build; fixed shapes for fixed (N, E_cap)):
    edge_index [2,E_cap] int64   row0 sender i, row1 receiver j (MACE: vec = pos[j]-pos[i]+shifts), sorted by
                                 receiver (dst), within a row strictly by sender (deterministic), padding at the end
    unit_shifts, shifts [E_cap,3] fp64
    rowptr_dst [N+1] int32       rowptr_dst[N] = E real (padding excluded); == rowptr_src (symmetric list)
    perm_dst [E_cap] int64       identity
    perm_src [E_cap] int64       src-sorted order, derived WITHOUT a sort: perm_src[e] = reverse edge of e (binary
                                 search of sender==dst(e) in row src(e)); identity on padding
    rowptr_dst_pad/_src_pad      same with last entry E_cap  ->  (perm_dst, rowptr_dst_pad, perm_src, rowptr_src_pad)
                                 is BITWISE EQUAL to nodetp8_bwd.csr.build_csr(edge_index, N) (tested every case)
    n_edges 0-d int64 (true E, may exceed E_cap), overflow 0-d int32 bits {1: E>E_cap, 2: bin overflow,
    4: reverse edge missing (appears together with 2)}, max_bin 0-d int32, cell/rcell/volume (as proto/stock)
  batch: tpl = BatchTemplate(calc, atoms)  (static tensors from a stock batch, like ProtoBuilder._template)
         bd = tpl.batch(out, positions, trim=False)  -> same keys/dtypes/values as ProtoBuilder.build except edge
         order; padded to E_cap (trim=True slices to E with ONE host sync, for testing/eager only). positions is
         used as given (no copy).
  Caller contract: check out["overflow"]==0 before trusting outputs (graph: read after replay; C owns policy).
    On E > E_cap rowptr is clamped to E_cap, n_edges is the true E -> resize to round_cap(1.2*n_edges).
    On bin overflow max_bin tells the needed bin_cap. Edges are never dropped silently.

PADDING  edges e in [E, E_cap): self-edge (N-1 -> N-1), unit_shift (m,0,0), shift = m*cell[0]; periodic
  m = max(1, ceil(2 r_max/|cell[0]|)); open m = 1 (extended cell row 0 length = extent+2r+1 > r). |vec| >= r_max ->
  polynomial envelope exactly 0 -> zero E/F/stress (also when MACE recomputes shifts from unit_shifts @ displaced
  cell). Last node -> dst and src order preserved. Verified: padded batch vs stock within tolerance (model rows).

SUPPORTED GEOMETRIES
  pbc all False: bounding box (min/max) recomputed on device each build; bin width max(r(1+1e-9), extent/bpd) per
    axis, at most bins_per_dim (default clamp(ceil(1.2 N^(1/3))+2, 4, 64)) per axis -> bins grow for expanding/sparse
    systems instead of overflowing the grid; extended cell/rcell/volume computed on device bitwise = proto/stock.
  pbc all True: orthorhombic or triclinic, every perpendicular height must give >= 3 bins of >= r_max(1+1e-9)
    (i.e. height >= ~15.0 A for r=5). Atoms anywhere (outside the cell, many cells away) -> wrapped on device.
  NotImplementedError (caller falls back to proto_graph): mixed pbc, < 3 bins per periodic dim (e.g. wbox192,
    L=12.4 A), degenerate cell, N<1.
CAPACITIES  E_cap (caller), bin_cap default: open 64; periodic max(64, round_up(0.25*bin_volume, 32)) (=64 for water;
  observed max_bin 24 for liquid water, 31 with injected boundary pairs); bins: periodic prod(nb), open bpd^3.
  memory (buffers): ~ 4*(nbins*bin_cap) + 52*N + 68*E_cap bytes (e.g. wbox5184: see TIMING table).

EXACTNESS (decisions bitwise identical to proto_graph, which is the GPU reference)
  open: d = pos[j]-pos[i]; periodic: w = floor(pos @ inv(cell)) (numpy inv), pw = pos - w@cell, d = (pw[j]-pw[i]) +
  img@cell (img table from the same torch matmul as proto); d2 = (dx^2 + dz^2) + dy^2 (torch's (d*d).sum(-1)
  reduction order -- probed, 0/4e6 mismatches); edge iff d2 < r*r; w@cell and S@cell computed as
  fma(a2,C2c,fma(a1,C1c,a0*C0c)) == cuBLAS fp64 [M,3]@[3,3] (probed bitwise M=1..3e5) -> shifts bitwise = proto
  even for triclinic + far-outside atoms. unit_shifts = (img - w[j]) + w[i] (referred to unwrapped positions).
  Known: stock matscipy uses an opaque different fp64 path: for pairs with |d - r_max| <= 2.7e-15 A (incl. d == r
  exactly, which matscipy includes) stock and proto/nl differ (boundary tests; such edges carry envelope weight ~0).
  Every non-constructed system: edge set AND unit_shifts AND shifts bitwise equal to stock and proto.
  Triclinic: frac = pos@inv uses non-FMA order (numpy CPU order unknown) -> w could differ from proto only for an
  atom within ~1 ulp of a cell face; S is then compensated by img, only ulp-boundary pairs could differ.

